        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "@drowning-cat, I was just about to add this as an example for 'mini.keymap', but noticed something. It only uses `map_combo` for a single character, which is a bit of an overkill.\n\nThis seems to be possible with a regular expression mapping something like this (of course, can be set locally only in HTML-like buffers):\n\n```lua\nlocal set_cursor_later = vim.schedule_wrap(function(pos) vim.api.nvim_win_set_cursor(0, pos) end)\n\nlocal auto_tag = function()\n  local row, col = unpack(vim.api.nvim_win_get_cursor(0))\n  local line = vim.api.nvim_get_current_line()\n\n  local tag = line:sub(1, col):match('<([%w:%-]+)[^<>]*$')\n  if tag == nil then return '>' end\n\n  set_cursor_later({ row, col + 1 })\n  return '></' .. tag .. '>'\nend\n\nvim.keymap.set('i', '>', auto_tag, { expr = true })\n```",
            "created_at": "2025-09-09T14:59:22Z",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/issues/752#issuecomment-3271118427",
