            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "> > I felt so smart before I read your message, but now I feel dumb again. Indeed, there is no actual reason to use `mini.keymap` here. Sorry for misleading you 😔\n> \n> [@drowning-cat](https://github.com/drowning-cat), there is nothing to feel dumb about :) The code worked and that what matters.\n> \n> > I use these in a FileType auto command, and this gets the job done very nicely.\n> \n> [@231tr0n](https://github.com/231tr0n), please create a dedicated autocommand with `pattern` set to the array of necessary filetypes. Something like:\n> \n> local autotag_ft = { 'svelte', 'vue', 'jsx', 'tsx', 'html', 'xml', 'xsl', 'javascriptreact', 'typescriptreact' }\n> local map_autotag = function()\n>   -- Code goes here\n> end\n> \n> local au_opts = { pattern = autotag_ft, callback = map_autotag, desc = 'Map autotag' }\n> vim.api.nvim_create_autocmd('FileType', au_opts)\n\nWell I have one big filetype autocommand which does everything from starting treesitter, setting folds, indentexpr. I taught of just sneaking this in to the same filetype autocommand so wrote in this way. But you are right. I will refactor this code in my actual config.",
