        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> I taught of just sneaking this in to the same filetype autocommand so wrote in this way.\n\nThen at least going the following route is less painful and more performant:\n\n```lua\nlocal autotag_map = {\n  svelte = true,\n  vue = true,\n  jsx = true,\n  tsx = true,\n  html = true,\n  xml = true,\n  xsl = true,\n  javascriptreact = true,\n  typescriptreact = true,\n}\n\nlocal a_big_callback = function(ev)\n  -- A very big callback\n\n  local ft = vim.bo[ev.buf].filetype\n  if autotag_map[ft] then\n    -- Map autotag\n  end\n\n  -- A very big callback continues\nend\n\nvim.api.nvim_create_autocmd('FileType', { callback = a_big_callback })\n```",
